      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LUVTOBEUPTOME (7) comes here following a Group One sixth two weeks ago over 2240m at Melton, beaten 14 metres by Enjoy Life. No surprise if he returned to his best form. THE GOLDEN HOOK (6) settled in the leading division before taking the lead and going on with the job to take out a 2070m race at Gawler last start, adding to his fine victory the run prior at Globe Derby Park. Stepping up a level this time but he is good enough to take this out. LISTEN TO THE HAND (5) is flying at present with two successive wins to his name, most recently at Gawler two weeks ago. Big chance to keep the ball rolling. DON CRUNCH (4) has been about the mark of late and must be respected, the latest offering a sound third at this track over 1790m.",
